WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.900
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.110
I'm introducing a new pilot who's 
been added to our squadron.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:12.280
She's arriving today from the 
Eastern European Dispatch Corps.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.280
I want you all to ensure she adjusts 
to the squadron as quickly as possible.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.030
Second Lieutenant Lise Hohenstein.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.470
Nice to meet you.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.070
Wait... Huh?!

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.550
Brother!

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.470
I've missed you all these years!

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.300
Is that you, Lise?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.370
10 Years Ago

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.520
Wait!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.610
East Berlin 
Kinderheim 115

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.600
Theodor!

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.990
Answer when your name is called!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.840
Sorry to keep you waiting, Theodor.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.870
I'm a distant relative of your mother's.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.970
I've been trying to find you for a long time.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.680
Welcome, Theodor.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:45.120
My wife, Marlene, and my daughter, Lise.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.930
You were born before she was, 
so you're her older brother.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.400
This is your home from now on.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.610
And from now on, you're part of our family.

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:00.310
Hello.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.030
I'm Lise Hohenstein.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.610
It's nice to meet you.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:33.140
I thought your sister was murdered 
three years ago by the Stasi.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.390
After I was released,

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:37.280
I searched everywhere for her.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.560
But I couldn't find her.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.530
Is it possible she's someone else?

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.740
That's Lise.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:48.340
It's creepy how this was 
just decided this morning.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:51.920
And the Stasi is monitoring our squadron.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:55.830
Wait, are you saying she's a Stasi informant?

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.420
She went missing, correct?

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.720
She may be a spy sent to 
the National People's Army.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.450
We can't ignore that she may have 
given in to torture or brainwashing.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.580
Lise wouldn't...

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.190
It's highly likely that you're her target.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.480
M-Me?

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:19.650
Their goal would be to bring you to 
their side and make you an informant.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.440
That's something the Stasi would do.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:24.950
We should question her.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.570
I'll make her talk.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.490
We need another pilot right now.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:34.140
Your naïveté makes me want to vomit.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.550
It's just that I don't want to imitate the Stasi.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.260
Theodor Eberbach,

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.130
find out what Second Lieutenant 
Lise Hohenstein is really up to.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.810
This is something only you can do.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:49.530
Roger.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.510
You're his adoptive sister?!

00:04:52.510 --> 00:04:54.350
No wonder you look nothing alike.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.180
I am his adoptive sister, 
but we're really siblings.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.870
I'm surprised all the women 
here are so pretty, though.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:11.830
You always did like blondes 
with nice figures, didn't you?

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.410
Like Captain Bernhard?

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.290
I-Idiot! What are you...

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.500
I once found a book of nude 
blondes under your bed.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.620
That was just something a classmate gave me!

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.300
I guess you're just a normal guy, after all.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.310
Shut up.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.970
Wh-What is it?

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.860
You're so cute!

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.170
I've always wanted a 
little sister like you, Katia.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:41.230
Because I was always the little sister.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.480
I hope you'll be friends 
with my brother and me.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.610
O-Okay...

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.960
I found you, Brother.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:05:59.560
Lise...

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.090
It's really you, right, Brother?

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.230
Yeah.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:12.970
I finally found you.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.730
That day, we were all arrested when
we tried to escape to West Germany.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.500
But you held my hand until the very end.

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:27.490
What happened to you after that?

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.400
I don't know.

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.580
I woke up in the hospital.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:36.200
That ribbon...

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.040
You remembered!

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.960
This is what kept me from giving up.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.730
I knew I'd see you again someday.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.560
What about you?

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:09.050
I was cast out alone, and joined 
the military in order to eat.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:13.070
I've fought my hardest ever since, 
while living in fear of the Stasi.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.590
Then why do you obey Captain Bernhard?

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.330
She's famous as a dog of the Stasi.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:24.630
That bitch turned in her family
so she alone could survive, right?

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.330
She's working with the men 
who killed Mom and Dad!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.250
She—

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.010
She's not like that.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:37.100
She informed on her brother because he 
was working against the government.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.850
Right now, Irisdina is more concerned about 
the country's future than anyone.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:45.780
And I don't know any commander that's better.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:47.410
You trust her?

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.150
Y-Yeah.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:51.860
I see.

00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:55.470
Then I'll trust her, too.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:57.660
Because you do.

00:07:57.890 --> 00:07:58.870
Lise...

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.790
I'm going to work my hardest from here on.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.790
I'll protect you, okay?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.250
S-Sure.

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.950
Well, goodnight, Brother.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.750
What are you doing out here?

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:21.940
N-Nothing.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:28.150
I'm glad you got to see your 
little sister again. Really.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.750
She might be a spy.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.360
That's what you think, too, right?

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.960
I'm sorry.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:38.840
When I saw how happy you looked, I...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:42.180
Sorry I made you keep it all to yourself.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.520
I think she might be a spy, too.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.420
Irisdina and Lieutenant Jeckeln do, as well.

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:52.440
I've been ordered to find out who she really is.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.220
So give me some time.

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:56.140
Theodor...

00:08:56.980 --> 00:08:59.170
She's my sister, and I love her.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.110
But you and I have a promise.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:02.880
Y-Yeah!

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:10.650
09, you're still too high.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.390
The Laser-classes will shoot you.

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:13.490
R-Roger.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.380
Not bad.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.060
You're good, Lise!

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:22.710
We never had to fly this low in my last squad.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.250
This is a training exercise! No talking!

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.920
S-Sorry!

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:33.460
<i>For a training exercise, 
we've gone pretty far today...</i>

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.440
Squadron leader, unknowns 
approaching from the rear.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.760
They're coming in fast.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:41.880
Wh-What's this sound?

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.130
Long-range missiles locking on us!

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.140
Is it... the Stasi?

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.990
Squadron leader, order us to break!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.180
Calm down.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.630
They're allies.

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.050
Attention, approaching unknowns.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.510
That's enough.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:59.750
If you stop now, I'll write it off as a joke.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.460
A joke?

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:02.810
They're mocking us.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.790
Who the hell are they?

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.170
Those are...

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:09.730
Tornadoes...

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:13.840
The West German 51st 
TSF Battalion, Huckebein!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.420
And... Tomcats!

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:20.440
The US Navy's 103rd Tactical Surface 
Fighter Strike Squadron,

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:21.720
the Jolly Rogers!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:25.060
What's the West doing here?

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.270
The US Navy's <i>Montana</i>-class...

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.360
And <i>Iowa</i>-class!

00:10:32.850 --> 00:10:35.070
And even the English <i>Lion</i>-class battleships!

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.070
Why are they all here?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.900
Attention, all units.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.950
Flight training is over.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:47.290
We will now represent East Germany 
in a UN Anti-BETA operation.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:57.230
Bornholm, Baltic Sea 
TSF Landing Craft <i>Peenemunde</i>

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:58.460
This is a major joint counterattack 
operation between the UN, the US,

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:03.350
the European Union Army, 
and the Warsaw Pact forces.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.260
Operation Neptune.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.180
The goal is to stabilize the military situation

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.460
on the continent by wiping out the BETA.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.110
First, we'll land on the beaches, 
to retake Gdansk Base

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:18.440
near the Polish coast and 
to secure a beachhead.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:24.240
Then we'll head farther inland and 
wipe out as many BETAs as we can.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:26.410
The US will take the northern sector.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:29.230
The European Union Army will take the center.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:34.000
And the Warsaw Pact forces will take the south.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:39.010
By sunset, each force will expand the 
beachhead by forty kilometers.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.550
After we bring the base and its 
defensive functions back on-line,

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.640
we'll switch to defending it.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.390
Forty kilometers?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:50.600
If this succeeds, East Germany 
will use the time this buys us

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.060
to greatly fortify our defenses.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.090
The West may be leading this operation,

00:11:56.090 --> 00:12:00.190
but don't forget that this fight will 
determine East Germany's future.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:04.190
I had no idea they were 
planning a mission like this.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.950
The West is doing this for its own reasons.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:12.460
They can't lose East Germany as a shield.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.420
That's why the comrade 
lieutenant is pissed off.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.000
Thirty ships.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.960
Five hundred TSFs.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.560
Thousands of tanks.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.920
Thirty thousand soldiers.

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:25.760
We're pretty tiny, aren't we?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.510
But if we can do something great,

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.610
we can show everyone East Germany's worth.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.890
And that's why we've been dispatched here,

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:37.130
as East Germany's best TSF squadron.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:44.010
No... Maybe there just aren't any real 
TSF squadrons left except for us.

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.590
So Lieutenant Jeckeln will lead Platoon 2,

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.290
with Katia, Lise, and me?

00:12:55.560 --> 00:13:01.050
This is because Lieutenant Pham is 
wounded and can't participate.

00:13:01.320 --> 00:13:06.400
Kid, are you capable of understanding 
the role you've been given?

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:11.230
The lieutenant doesn't have much combat 
experience, so I'll assist her,

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:15.910
while protecting Katia and trying to learn 
the connection between Lise and the Stasi.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.330
Now that you're one of our comrades,

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:22.140
you will have other missions beyond a pilot's.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:23.990
Consider this the training for that.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.000
The captain expects you to succeed.

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:32.290
Then I will.

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:37.170
Former Polish People's Republic Territory 
Gdansk Bay

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:57.280
62% of BETAs on the coast have been destroyed.

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:59.770
Surface strike force will continue its assault.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:03.650
120 seconds until the TSFs begin their attack.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:08.150
TSFs are to take care not to cross 
the line of fire when jumping.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.230
<i>Fuhlendorf</i> has been hit.

00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:19.370
It's sinking.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.000
Don't worry.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.700
The Laser-classes on the coast won't 
last long against this barrage.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:26.680
Don't be afraid.

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.570
<i>Klausdorf</i>, sunk.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.640
No...

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.930
All units, have you heard this one?

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:37.640
Someone sent in a question 
to a Berlin radio station.

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.940
"Can you eat a BETA corpse?"

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:43.900
And the guy on the radio said,

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.470
"They're far too disgusting to eat.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:50.040
Unless you're English."

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:53.930
Katia, Lise...

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:57.080
We'll support the comrade lieutenant, 
and ensure the mission's success.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:58.970
Roger.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.150
Comrade Second Lieutenant...

00:15:00.150 --> 00:15:02.040
Th-Thank you.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.550
<i>Your abilities as a commander, huh?</i>

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:10.550
Attention, all units.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:15.680
Our squadron will now work with UN 
forces to expand the beachhead

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.180
and secure the safety of our rear forces.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:26.440
666th TSF Squadron, take off!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.620
Flagship of the GDR Navy 
<i>Karl Marx</i>

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:40.620
The 666th Squadron has reached 
designated area and initiated combat.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.010
You worried, miss?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.520
No, my squad is the strongest in East Germany.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:50.800
They'll carry out their mission. I know it.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.920
I hope so, too.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.240
Of course.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.180
That's why we brought you.

00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:00.610
Yes, Comrade Major Zweig.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:03.190
What's the overall situation?

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:09.250
The US forces to the north and EU forces at 
the center are proceeding as planned.

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:13.240
But our forces to the south are 
falling a little behind.

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.230
Make them hurry.

00:16:14.230 --> 00:16:15.950
Don't let the West get ahead of us.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:18.700
Gdansk 
Southern Beachhead

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.390
Okay, we'll take down this pack.

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:24.960
Comrade Second Lieutenant 
Eberbach, back me up!

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:26.180
Roger.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:29.250
Katia, circle around from the right.

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.630
Lise, help her.

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:39.480
Lise, we're going to move. Come with me.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:44.000
Lise?

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.730
Lise!

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.750
Katia!

00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:00.020
Sorry! I lost sight of you!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.770
Are you okay, Katia?

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:03.460
Th-Thank you.

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:07.190
I'm glad I made it in time...

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:07.960
Lise!

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.280
Lise...

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.210
Attention, all units.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:13.420
We'll take a quick break here.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:16.220
Everyone, check your magazines.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.530
This will be a long fight. Rest while you can.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.660
What are you thinking, Comrade Captain?!

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:23.080
I'm overriding that order!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:26.760
We've been ordered to expand the
beachhead forty kilometers by sunset!

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:31.040
If we fall behind the US and EU, 
it will damage East Germany's reputation.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.430
That means we'll—

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:35.990
Another BETA corps has appeared.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:37.660
They're passing through 
the ruins of Tczew City.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.910
They number over ten thousand, 
with multiple Laser-classes.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:41.890
Damn it.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:44.580
That's near the boundary between us and the EU.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.940
What are they doing?

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:51.460
Tell UN Command that we're initiating 
bombardment of the target area.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.570
That's crazy!

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:55.640
If we open fire without knowing 
where our allies are...

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:57.340
We need to stop the enemy advance.

00:17:57.730 --> 00:18:00.970
If we don't, they'll be here very soon.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:03.050
Intercept the BETA?

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.930
There are ten thousand!

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:08.730
And the heavy-metal clouds mean we 
don't know where the other units are!

00:18:08.990 --> 00:18:10.550
We only need to delay them.

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.730
If we lose the beachhead, it's over.

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:15.330
We're about three thousand 
meters from enemy lines.

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:17.710
We will head toward them and delay them.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:19.800
Lieutenant Jeckeln, you have the rear.

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:21.120
I know.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:21.990
All units, get to it!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.670
Okay, we've stopped them.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:40.300
All units, aim for the unarmored spots!

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:50.520
Damn it, there are too many.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.060
The rear unit is to split up and attack.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.010
Don't let a single one through!

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.650
No, Comrade Lieutenant!

00:18:56.950 --> 00:18:59.980
More are coming. 
They'll isolate and destroy us!

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:02.050
Don't argue with my order!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.120
Just shut up and obey!

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:07.310
Tornadoes?

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:09.080
Why so few?

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.940
That's an artillery recon unit...

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:16.300
I-Incoming artillery fire! 
We need to get out of here!

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:19.270
Artillery? What are you talking about?

00:19:19.270 --> 00:19:20.820
We're in the middle of the BETA!

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:25.380
The West didn't anticipate anyone engaging 
the BETA in close combat like we have.

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:28.470
They always try to lay down as much 
artillery fire as possible first.

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:31.030
Then we...

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:33.570
I'm sure that's it.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:34.400
Damn it!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:37.310
Comrade Lieutenant, we need to get out of here!

00:19:37.310 --> 00:19:38.640
That's ridiculous.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:42.280
If we withdraw, that means admitting 
the West's strategy is superior.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.620
For the Fatherland's sake, we can't!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.950
Now isn't the time for that!

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.820
You want us all to die here?

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.120
Attention, all units.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.070
We're leaving now.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.840
Are you sane, Comrade Captain?

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:01.170
Staying here in this situation is simple folly.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:05.850
Our attack on the Destroyer-class 
has already shown our strength.

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:09.160
We still haven't fulfilled our political objective!

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.640
Do you want them to doubt our party loyalty?!

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:16.590
The destruction of the 666th, East Germany's 
strongest TSF squad, would be

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.790
far greater treason against the Fatherland.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:23.250
Surface-fleet bombardment incoming.

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:37.960
You TSFs...

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.520
If you can hear me, head north.

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:41.460
We'll cover your escape.

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:42.710
Thank you.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:48.430
I am Captain Irisdina Bernhard, of the 
East German 666th TSF Squadron.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:53.810
This is Major Joachim Balck, of the West 
German 51st Tactical Armor Battalion.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:56.810
We'll handle the Grapplers to the rear!

00:20:57.140 --> 00:20:58.980
All units, jump!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.050
Roger!

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:04.990
Hurry, Comrade Lieutenant.

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:10.450
Roger Leader to all units.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.950
Four thousand meters to target.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:13.820
All units, fire on my signal.

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:16.620
Let those monsters taste our Phoenixes!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.000
Yes, sir!

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:20.210
Light 'em up!

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.090
Wow...

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:34.560
Those are the US Military's Phoenix missiles.

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:36.800
High-tech, long-range guided missiles.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.310
The ones they used to lock on us.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:41.030
This can't be happening...

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:43.790
This was supposed to be our job.

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.570
You understand now, right?

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:50.530
This is how East Germany, how the 
socialist countries, are treated.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:53.210
The whole world hates us.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:30.310
Gdansk 
Boundary Between Southern and Central Zones

00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:30.310
You okay, Crystal?

00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:32.800
I-I'm fine...

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:38.840
Captain, why did we have to sustain 
losses to save those people?

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:41.310
Crystal almost died!

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:44.090
We couldn't let them die.

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:45.690
They're Germans, same as us.

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:46.880
Same as us?

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:51.820
I refuse to accept that people 
like them are German.

00:23:51.820 --> 00:23:55.750
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:52.230 --> 00:23:53.400
I refuse!
